title: $:/plugins/pankesh/myTiddlyEncryption/readme

! MyTiddlyEncryption

Per-tiddler AES-256 encryption for TiddlyWiki v5. Each tiddler can be independently encrypted with its own password (or share a password with other tiddlers using the same ''prompt label'').

!! Quick Start

# Tag any tiddler with `Encrypt(myLabel)` — replace `myLabel` with a short hint to help you remember the password
# Save the wiki — you will be prompted for a password for that label
# The tiddler text is encrypted and the tag changes to `Decrypt(myLabel)`
# To read it again, click the ''Decrypt'' button in the toolbar or tiddler body

!! Shared Passwords

Multiple tiddlers tagged with the same label (e.g. `Encrypt(work)`) share one password. You are only asked once per label per session.

!! Widgets

Place these in any tiddler to create action buttons:

|!Widget |!Description |
|`<$tiddlyencrypt-decrypt tiddler="Title"/>` |Decrypt a single tiddler |
|`<$tiddlyencrypt-decryptall/>` |Decrypt all encrypted tiddlers (prompts for each unique label) |
|`<$tiddlyencrypt-decryptall prompt="work"/>` |Decrypt only tiddlers with the `work` label |
|`<$tiddlyencrypt-changepw prompt="work"/>` |Change the password for all tiddlers sharing the `work` label |

!! Configuration

|!Setting |!Tiddler |!Default |
|Show Decrypt button inside tiddler body |`$:/config/pankesh/myTiddlyEncryption/ShowDecryptInContent` |`yes` |

Set the value to `no` to show the Decrypt button only in the toolbar.

!! Notes

* Passwords are held in memory for the current browser session only — they are never saved to disk
* Encrypted tiddlers use AES-256-CCM via TiddlyWiki's built-in SJCL library
* The encrypted storage format is: `TWEncrypted:v1` followed by a JSON blob
* If you forget a password, the tiddler content cannot be recovered
* To change a password: use `<$tiddlyencrypt-changepw prompt="label"/>`, then save
